WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:03.970
Film Courage: Alex, when you teach actors, what lessons are you trying to drive home

00:00:03.970 --> 00:00:05.960
to them?

00:00:05.960 --> 00:00:08.960
Either creatively, personally?

00:00:08.960 --> 00:00:18.640
Alex Sol: If I’m directing a play, I’m
trying to show the person that’s doing the

00:00:18.640 --> 00:00:30.890
part, the work that there is a difference
between you know acting something and being

00:00:30.890 --> 00:00:37.989
a human being and experiencing something,
sharing yourself.

00:00:37.989 --> 00:00:44.989
What I’m trying to say is, from what this
was for me, why I got into it was the notion

00:00:44.989 --> 00:00:49.340
that I could honestly share myself for other
people.

00:00:49.340 --> 00:00:53.719
That human transaction was what it was all
about.

00:00:53.719 --> 00:00:54.719
Period.

00:00:54.719 --> 00:00:56.510
End of story.

00:00:56.510 --> 00:00:58.000
That is what it was about.

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:04.379
So when I direct a play I try to maximize
the human experience of being a person and

00:01:04.379 --> 00:01:06.170
what that really feels like.

00:01:06.170 --> 00:01:11.700
And what that really sounds like is very different
when someone’s telling the truth versus

00:01:11.700 --> 00:01:15.680
I’m clever and I know how to act something.

00:01:15.680 --> 00:01:20.520
And that experience when you have the human
experience, it transcends like...that’s

00:01:20.520 --> 00:01:22.450
a good actor.

00:01:22.450 --> 00:01:26.420
It transcends that you affected me personally.

00:01:26.420 --> 00:01:29.259
Do you understand what I am saying?

00:01:29.259 --> 00:01:39.280
So that... what I would say is get real with
yourself and tell the truth in your work.

00:01:39.280 --> 00:01:40.280
That is what I would say.

00:01:40.280 --> 00:01:40.780
Question: What was the last acting performance
you saw that really affected you?

